Nethack is a difficult game - this goes without saying. And sometimes
it seems to have a mind of it's own.

Never before have I had a run of such extreme good and bad luck as to
make the RNG seem not only to be particularly cruel but actually
thoughtfully sadistic. This is a tragic story of woe - do not continue
reading this post if you can't stomach tragedy of mythic proportion.

The scene: having recently ascended for the first time because of an
early WoW I expected it to be a long time until I found another one
before the castle. Not so! A promising young Samurai found one on
level 9 and had visions of a second ascension. I wished up some SDSM
and some Speed boots and then a wandering Mountain nymph walked up -
bold as brass - and stole everything.

Of course this meant war. I realised that if I hunted down this
particular nymph I would have a damn good chance of ascension - I
couldn't let this setback get in my way. Unfortunately I hadn't picked
up telepathy yet so I had to walk around the level until I happened
upon her. When I did I whipped out my yumi, took aim and  - had all
weapons stolen. Now it was desperate - I was deep in the dungeon with
no means of self defence... I picked up a few rocks and continued in
earnest.

Met the nymph again, hurled rocks - had my last piece of armour
stolen! AC of 10, no weapons and I *knew* that the RNG was preparing
some nasties for me.

A pony! The war of attrition starts! Luckily I had just read a
spellbook of healing so I managed to dispatch the thing (with
judicious use of the 'E' word and lots of luck). More frantic
searching.

A swarm of killer bees! Of course! Nothing less could be expected of
the fun loving RNG. Careful use of my legs allowed me to evade the
encounter.

A dwarf lord! Hostile! With a mattock! More careful use of the 'E'
word and legs...
And to top it off a horde of hill orcs. I wanted to cry.

What followed was a blur of healing, prayer and the E word.
Unbelievably I was answered favourably 3 times in quick succession and
unbelievably I was alive at the end with dead bees, dwarf and orcs
surrounding me! I grabbed the mattock and all the armour I could find
(I didn't care if it was cursed) and finally managed to off the
nymph...

Except she didn't have my stuff... Something was very wrong with this
picture. I guess I just had to look around...

Slowly it dawned on me: the RNG's diabolical plan came to light. In
order to infuse me with hope it allowed me to find a WoW and to even
defeat a nymph. All along however it had kept the terrible truth from
me: there were three nymphs on this level. I had killed one but there
were two left to torment me.

I battled on. The mattock was stolen. I kept at it, slowly hunting
down the nymphs and whittling away. The second nymph went down! Once
again - not the right nymph. She had some dwarfish boots on her which
helped my AC though...

Notice how the RNG played me: at every disaster I was able to recover
just enough to give me hope that there would be a happy ending (a
happy ending??? In nethack?? Okay - so I'm naive).

In the corridors hot on the trail I turned a corner and:
You are frozen by the floating eye's gaze!

That should've been it - you never survive floating eyes. I tapped
enter a few times and the friendly neighbourhood nymph appeared and
fleeced me of more stuff. Then I was free! I had survived a floating
eye encounter with low AC in a deepish dungeon level!

I quickly turned down a corridor branch to avoid the eye when:
You are frozen by the floating eye's gaze!

And that was the final straw. 3 Nymphs and 2 floating eyes and the
death blow was given by a passing iguana (the ignominy!). Just enough
to ruin your day and skillfully plotted by the RNG.

I do not blame the eyes nor the iguana - they were mere pawns. But the
nymphs - they have to go...

And this is why the very next ?oG I find is going straight into some
Holy Water and I'm going to genocide every last nymph. Wait! Even
better - I'm going to stock pile a ton of ?oG go to Sokoban and then
I'm personally, with my bare hands, going to send them to extinction.
*Then* I'll genocide them for good measure. Grrr...



